// The shapefit package: deterministic instruments for deciding how to shape a
// mesh. A program reaches it with 'import shapefit', and gets:
//
// - Fits (fits.cone, forms.cone): 'fitPlane', 'fitSphere', 'fitEllipsoidAxis'
//   (axes along x, y, z), 'fitEllipsoid' (any orientation), 'fitQuadric' (the
//   general quadric, with 'quadricKind' to name it), 'fitCylinder' and
//   'fitCapsule', each by least squares over a region's points with optional
//   weights, returning a Form: its parameters and the weighted RMS and greatest
//   residual. 'formDistance' is the signed distance from a point to a form.
//   'gather' takes a mesh's vertices by number.
// - Curvature (curvature.cone): 'curvature' gives every vertex's principal
//   curvatures and directions (Rusinkiewicz 2004); 'classifyVertices' names each
//   patch dome, cup, saddle, ridge, valley or flat; 'curvatureChannels' stores
//   them in the mesh.
// - Residuals (residual.cone): 'residualToForm' and 'residualToMesh' give each
//   vertex's signed distance from a fitted form or another mesh;
//   'regionStats' summarises any per-vertex field per region (a face set or a
//   channel).
// - Landmark correspondence (align.cone): 'alignPoints' (rigid, or similarity with
//   scale, by Horn's quaternion method) from point pairs; 'icp' refines it against
//   a surface with trimming.
// - Features on a field (features.cone): 'findPeaks', 'findPits' and
//   'findCreases' (ridge and valley lines).
// - Silhouettes (silhouette.cone): orthographic outlines from several views as
//   polygons, with no renderer, compared by IoU and Hausdorff distance.
// - Pictures (picture.cone): a software canvas that draws shaded meshes coloured
//   per vertex, outlines and markers, and saves PNGs; 'drawMeshLit' under a
//   'Lighting' rig fixed to the view (key, fill, soft highlight), so two shapes
//   drawn in one view are lit alike.
// - Synthetic shapes (shapes.cone): spheres, cylinders, capsules and height grids
//   whose true form is known, for tests.
//
// Everything runs in a fixed order in f64 where it matters, so the same input
// gives the same bits on every machine.

mod shapefit;

import libc;
import geomath use *;
import collections use *;
import mesh use *;
import imagedecode use *;
import fs;
import path use Path;
